{"id":1030,"date":"2023-10-23T06:32:35","date_gmt":"2023-10-23T06:32:35","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/franziskaiseli.com\/?p=1030"},"modified":"2024-06-20T09:00:16","modified_gmt":"2024-06-20T09:00:16","slug":"morning-musings-navigating-the-delicate-balance-opinions-respect-and-shared-humanity","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/franziskaiseli.com\/2023\/10\/23\/morning-musings-navigating-the-delicate-balance-opinions-respect-and-shared-humanity\/","title":{"rendered":"Morning Musings: Navigating the Delicate Balance: Opinions, Respect, and Shared Humanity"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-1031\" src=\"https:\/\/franziskaiseli.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/10\/IMG_4906-300x225.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"508\" height=\"381\" srcset=\"https:\/\/franziskaiseli.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/10\/IMG_4906-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/franziskaiseli.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/10\/IMG_4906-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/franziskaiseli.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/10\/IMG_4906-768x576.jpg 768w, https:\/\/franziskaiseli.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/10\/IMG_4906-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/franziskaiseli.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/10\/IMG_4906-2048x1536.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/franziskaiseli.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/10\/IMG_4906-510x382.jpg 510w, https:\/\/franziskaiseli.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/10\/IMG_4906-1080x810.jpg 1080w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 508px) 100vw, 508px\" \/><\/p>\n<p>Every morning, I take our dog Rosie for a peaceful beach walk before the<br \/>\ncraziness of the day.<\/p>\n<p>I truly cherish spending this time reflecting as I miss the philosophical<br \/>\nengagements with my Swiss friends\u2026 so instead\u2026 I have philosophical<br \/>\ndiscussions in my mind.<\/p>\n<p>Today, given all the chaos, inhumanity and irrationality in the world, my thoughts<br \/>\ngravitated towards the delicate balance between opinion (and beliefs) and<br \/>\nrespect for each other.<\/p>\n<p>We all hold opinions, subjective interpretations of our world that are not the<br \/>\ntruth. These opinions, formed and moulded by our upbringing and life<br \/>\nexperiences, become beliefs when reinforced repeatedly. They are our<br \/>\nperception of life.<\/p>\n<p>Here\u2019s the paradox I\u2019m observing: There\u2019s a difference between mutable<br \/>\nopinions and enduring principles. For instance, a principle such as &#8216;always<br \/>\nrespond with kindness&#8217; is likely to remain constant over time and most of us<br \/>\nadhere to such principles. Yet\u2026 people\u2019s opinions and actions, despite living by a<br \/>\nprinciple of kindness, may not always mirror this tenet. Depending on the<br \/>\nsituation, our opinions and actions might deviate from kindness\u2026 be it because<br \/>\nthe other person has another belief, another religion, another background,<br \/>\nanother story, another perspective\u2026<\/p>\n<p>Is it possible then, to maintain our opinions, yet respect differing perspectives\u2026<br \/>\npossibly reducing conflict? Absolutely! Is it easy? Not in the slightest.<\/p>\n<p>It takes courage and awareness to honour and respect other\u2019s opinions,<br \/>\nespecially if they are the opposite of ours. It takes courage to confess when<br \/>\nwe&#8217;re mistaken, or to change our own opinion as it might disrupt our identity.<br \/>\nRespect, fundamentally, is about finding common ground\u2026 and our shared<br \/>\nhumanity is the most basic of these\u2026 we are all human (or so I thought. A<br \/>\ndiscussion for another day).<\/p>\n<p>*Disclaimer: The musings above reflect my opinion, yours may differ from mine<br \/>\nand that\u2019s when interesting discussions and learnings ensue if we treat each<br \/>\nother with respect. You are free to agree, disagree, or be ambivalent about the<br \/>\nabove.<\/p>\n<p>Or as author Simone Elkeles eloquently put it, &#8220;Opinions are like a-holes,<br \/>\neveryone has one.&#8221;<\/p>\n<p>Either way, I\u2019d love to hear your thoughts on this.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Every morning, I take our dog Rosie for a peaceful beach walk before the craziness of the day. I truly cherish spending this time reflecting as I miss the philosophical engagements with my Swiss friends\u2026 so instead\u2026 I have philosophical discussions in my mind. Today, given all the chaos, inhumanity and irrationality in the world, [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":1031,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_et_pb_use_builder":"","_et_pb_old_content":"","_et_gb_content_width":"","disable_featured_image":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-1030","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-uncategorized"],"aioseo_notices":[],"aioseo_head":"\n\t\t<!-- All in One SEO 5.0.1.1 - aioseo.com -->\n\t<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Every morning, I take our dog Rosie for a peaceful beach walk before the craziness of the day. I truly cherish spending this time reflecting as I miss the philosophical engagements with my Swiss friends\u2026 so instead\u2026 I have philosophical discussions in my mind. Today, given all the chaos, inhumanity and irrationality in the world,\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"max-image-preview:large\" \/>\n\t<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/franziskaiseli.com\/2023\/10\/23\/morning-musings-navigating-the-delicate-balance-opinions-respect-and-shared-humanity\/\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"generator\" content=\"All in One SEO (AIOSEO) 5.0.1.1\" \/>\n\t\t<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n\t\t<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Franziska Iseli -\" \/>\n\t\t<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n\t\t<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Morning Musings: Navigating the Delicate Balance: O